# Invert Polarity: "Choose target spell, then flip a coin. If you win the flip, gain control of that spell and you may choose
# new targets for it. If you lose the flip, counter that spell." Bot2's Lightning Bolt aims at Bot1 and Bot1 answers it
# with Invert Polarity. The flip is a two-sided die, which a scenario's [Dice] fixes; here it is lost (the second face), so the Bolt is
# countered and goes to Bot2's graveyard without touching Bot1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Island
Invert Polarity
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x3
Mountain x12

[Dice]
2

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Invert Polarity.Cast(Lightning Bolt)
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Invert Polarity
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
